1
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,320
(A few weeks ago)

2
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:25,040
Brother Kin, we have been following
that rich lady.

3
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:28,240
She jogs near her villa every night
at around 10 o'clock.

4
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:30,600
That's too early.

5
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,720
Clear Water Bay is a rich neighborhood.

6
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:34,200
Nobody is out and about after 8 o'clock.

7
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:36,520
That woman lives near the hillside

8
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:39,800
where there's no CCTV and quite dark
with few street lamps.

9
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,000
We can ambush her right there.

10
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,120
The client is paying USD$500K

11
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,120
and wants her dead.

12
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:49,080
That's easy...I'll grab her by the neck
from behind

13
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:51,480
and stab her a dozen times.

14
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:53,240
That should kill her.

15
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,480
Or we bring a chainsaw

16
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,720
and cut her up right here...

17
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,600
Dummy can make a video.

18
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,800
I'll tell the client
once the Boss gets paid,

19
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,040
we'll take action.

20
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,680
Wait for my order.

21
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,560
Good!

22
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,480
Morning, gentlemen!

23
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,720
Sorry, Brother Kin! I overslept again.

24
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,000
You're in a meeting?

25
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,200
Let me record this...

26
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,120
What are you talking about?

27
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,360
A hit.

28
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,040
What recording? Are you nuts?

29
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,800
You told me I'm the secretary,

30
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:29,960
I came down without putting makeup on.

31
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:30,840
Don't get on my case.

32
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:34,200
Brother Kin is not scolding you.

33
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,560
You're so pretty even without makeup...

34
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,840
You skin is so fair...

35
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:43,400
Your skin is smooth as tofu...

36
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:44,920
Cut the crap!

37
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:47,840
They're probably hungry.

38
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,040
Let's order afternoon tea.

39
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:50,560
Are you on the menu?
Hey...

40
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,240
Do they have rice noodles?

41
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,480
Do it over there.

42
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:54,680
We still have business to discuss.

43
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:55,640
Rice noodles?

44
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:02,040
What's the story with the bank?

45
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,200
We've been doing site survey
for a few days.

46
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,360
Cops don't go out there during the day.

47
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,720
We can take action any time.

48
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
I have the tools ready.

49
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:13,280
I mapped out the getaway route.

50
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,920
OK, let's do it tomorrow.

51
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,520
Stay on your toes

52
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,360
and get me a few hundred thousand.

53
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,480
We have a pretty suitcase.

54
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:32,000
Miss, planning a trip lately?

55
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,680
Just fill out this form for the suitcase.

56
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,120
Miss, have you heard of a virtual bank?

57
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:38,680
A virtual bank is also a bank.

58
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,640
A virtual credit card is still
a credit card.

59
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,760
The upside is you don't need a physical card

60
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:44,040
so you won't need to worry about it
being stolen.

61
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:45,800
When you apply for the card,

62
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:46,880
we'll give a pretty suitcase.

63
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:47,680
Sign your pretty name here

64
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,920
and you'll get the pretty suitcase.

65
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,880
It's OK...
Thanks!

66
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,320
Just fill this out...

67
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,920
Miss, you wish to apply for
this virtual credit card?

68
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:02,720
If I apply for it, I'll get this suitcase?

69
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,160
Yes, but while stocks last.

70
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,320
I want to apply.

71
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,760
Please come this way. Your ID card please?

72
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:12,480
A photocopy? Is that OK?

73
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,720
Should be OK...
Good!

74
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,400
It's just a recognizance form.

75
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:19,520
It's still proof of identity.

76
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,080
Stop toying with us, Miss Hong.

77
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,440
I should get my ID card soon.

78
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,920
When you get your official ID card,

79
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:26,880
you can look us up.

80
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,480
But I really want this suitcase.

81
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,720
I also want my own credit card.

82
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,520
Can you help me register for it now

83
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:34,840
and I'll submit the ID later?

84
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:35,960
We'll wait for you.

85
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:39,520
Sir, would you like to apply for
a virtual credit card?

86
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:46,920
After the whole morning,

87
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,320
We only have a dozen applications.

88
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,840
He wants a few hundred thousand?

89
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,560
We won't get much from selling this data.

90
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:52,920
What are you doing?

91
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,680
They needed the information

92
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,880
to borrow from loan sharks.

93
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:57,720
Why don't we do it ourselves?

94
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:58,640
(Loan application)

95
00:04:58,760 --> 00:04:59,280
(Loan amount : $400,000)

96
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,760
Are you crazy? $400K?

97
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,920
I thought only small amounts
will be approved

98
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:06,360
without checking and meeting
the applicant.

99
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,840
You must take a chance.

100
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,560
What's the point of breaking the law?

101
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,160
Brother Kin would have been more vicious.

102
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:15,280
He's vicious if we screwed up.

103
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,360
Are you scared now?

104
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:21,040
Just pass everything to Brother Kin
and let him decide.

105
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,120
He just summoned us.

106
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:28,400
We made money on the bank job.

107
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:31,800
The Boss saw how hard you worked.

108
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:35,520
Here's your bonus...

109
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,240
Thanks, Brother Kin...

110
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,080
Yeah! You're so brilliant!

111
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,800
Who's more brilliant? Me or him?

112
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,640
Get lost! Stop taking advantage of her.

113
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,960
Suet, never mind this scumbag.

114
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,520
Speak for yourself...

115
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,440
Shut up, you two.

116
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:52,400
Order some shooters for us.

117
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:52,960
Right!

118
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,040
Suet, what would you like?

119
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,360
I'll let you decide.
Let me decide?

120
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,760
Let's go...
OK...

121
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:02,200
I didn't forget about you.

122
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,080
This is your share.

123
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:08,640
How come I get a bigger stack
then Dummy and Shek?

124
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:10,000
Thanks, Brother Kin!

125
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,120
Will they be unhappy about this?

126
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:15,000
Don't be silly! They're happy to see you.

127
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,720
You've been a big help.

128
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:19,680
My turn...
Drink up...

129
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,640
OK!

130
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:24,720
Brother Kin is next...ten...

131
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:25,760
That's awesome...

132
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,360
That's cheating...
Drain the glass...

133
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,480
I will...

134
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,960
Hurry up...
Open the door!

135
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,880
What's taking so long? Drink...

136
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:38,600
OK...I'll let you go first...

137
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,840
Miss, are you OK?

138
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,280
I feel dizzy.

139
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,200
Let me help you over there.

140
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:37,760
You have any chronic illnesses
or on any medication?

141
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,360
I'm a nurse. Anything I can help you with?

142
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:41,040
I'm fine.

143
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:43,320
My hospital is nearby.

144
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,760
Let me take you there for a checkup.

145
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:51,680
Other than feeling dizzy,

146
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,840
you feel anything else?

147
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:55,080
I don't know.

148
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,880
Did you eat or drink anything?

149
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:00,880
I was drinking last night.

150
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,720
You have any drug allergies?

151
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,520
I guess not...I don't know.

152
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:08,640
Cathy!

153
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,000
How is she?

154
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:13,560
She said she might have had
too much to drink last night.

155
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:15,480
She doesn't know anything else.

156
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,760
Your BP is very low.

157
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,360
Have you eaten this morning?

158
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:23,120
When was your last period?

159
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:27,480
I think...I don't remember.

160
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,360
Is it possible you're pregnant?

161
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:31,880
A baby! Of course not!

162
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,920
I'm on the pill. I don't have a baby.

163
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,200
Miss, you can't leave yet.

164
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:39,000
I said I'm fine. I just had too much
to drink.

165
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,600
But your BP is very low.

166
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:43,000
Your SBP is 90 and DBP is only 55.

167
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,320
You should stay and see a doctor.

168
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:47,040
Don't be such a pain.

169
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,800
It's my duty to remind you.

170
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,120
Wait...

171
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:54,280
I don't have money on me.

172
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,080
Can you loan me some money?

173
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:59,040
Nurse Tse? I'll pay you back later.

174
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,200
I have money to loan you.

175
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,120
But I really think you need
a thorough checkup...

176
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:24,840
Look!

177
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,120
Is it new?

178
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:30,800
I personally tested it when I came to work.

179
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,480
The response of the control is quick,

180
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,680
very steady when you go up and down hill.

181
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,760
I already have one.

182
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:40,960
But this one is electric.

183
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,080
It's so much more convenient.

184
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:43,520
I think you should try

185
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,080
going outside for some sun.

186
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:48,880
I can't even leave the hospital,

187
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,480
let alone go outside for some sun.

188
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:53,600
I recently read an article

189
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:57,280
about someone with GBS,
Guillain-Barre Syndrome like you,

190
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:00,040
after a few years' treatment,

191
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:02,920
had a full recovery.

192
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:06,480
But this person worked very hard in rehab.

193
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:08,560
I think if you tried harder,

194
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,920
maybe someday, you can recover too

195
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,160
and leave this hospital

196
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,720
without the use of a wheelchair.

197
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:16,800
You sounded like I was lazy.

198
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:23,360
I have done all sorts of treatment.

199
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:26,800
You should know since you took care of me.

200
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,440
I know you've been good.

201
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:35,480
That's why I think it's so unfair.

202
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:39,320
I just saw this girl today,

203
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,360
she's young and running around,

204
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:44,280
but got so drunk in broad daylight

205
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,920
she had no clue what she was doing.

206
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,200
She was wasting her life away.

207
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:53,320
And you...who was so happy

208
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,240
with a family and a career

209
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:58,200
but plagued with this illness.

210
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:03,480
What's wrong?

211
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:08,200
Nothing. Ben hasn't been here in four days.

212
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,160
Has it been that long?

213
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:14,240
I always mark it down. I can't be wrong.

214
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,360
Maybe he's busy. Just call him.

215
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,000
Better not bother him.

216
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,480
I have nothing to do,

217
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,720
so I'm counting the days.

218
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:25,280
He's so busy, he doesn't have to be here.

219
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:30,240
But you...if you have time,
please keep me company

220
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,360
so I won't be so bored.

221
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:32,960
OK!

222
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,960
I can spend time with Mary on Tuesday.

223
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:48,760
Cathy, next Tuesday is your day off.

224
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,800
Can you take Nurse Chow's shift?

225
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,040
She said something came up at home

226
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:52,840
and she must take the day off.

227
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,200
But I can't find a substitute.

228
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,800
I can.

229
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:02,720
Thank you.

230
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,200
Nurse Tse!

231
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,920
Mr. Lau, you finally showed up.

232
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,320
Your wife said you haven't been here
for a few days.

233
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,280
She really missed you.

234
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:18,600
Has Mary been able to sleep?

235
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:19,760
Does she still have insomnia?

236
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:21,800
The doctor prescribed something
to calm her nerves.

237
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,800
She was able to sleep better.

238
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,760
Don't worry, it's quite mild

239
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:27,840
and won't have side effects.

240
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,040
Thank you. Thanks for looking after her.

241
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,880
Hurry inside. She's waiting.

242
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:32,600
Thank you.

243
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:44,040
Did I wake you?

244
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:44,920
Honey!

245
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,360
Get some sleep. I'll just sit with you.

246
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:50,520
I can sleep any time I want.

247
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:53,120
I don't get to see enough of you.

248
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,800
Sorry, I've been busy at work.

249
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,720
But I have nothing to do tonight.

250
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,400
I can stay as long as I like.

251
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:11,400
The creamy almond tea with egg white
smells really good.

252
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,560
I knew you liked it last time.

253
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:18,720
But it's not near your office.

254
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,400
You shouldn't go out of your way to get it.

255
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:23,560
It's on my way today.

256
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,800
Get some rest.

257
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:31,520
Drive carefully.

258
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,520
I've been busy at work.

259
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,120
I'll come again in a few days.

260
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:39,880
It's OK. Focus on work. Don't worry about me

261
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:41,040
Get some rest.

262
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,480
Honey?

263
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,560
Nurse Tse takes really good care of me.

264
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,440
Especially when you're not around.

265
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:53,840
She spends her personal time with me.

266
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:57,440
If possible, please thank her for me.

267
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:59,640
I will. Bye!

268
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,240
It smells great!

269
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:17,440
You bet! You bought me this jasmine perfume.

270
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,960
I know you like the smell of jasmine.

271
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:26,000
Let's take a spin in the car

272
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,800
and get out of the city.

273
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,760
Good! It's not every day we have
the day off together.

274
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:33,520
Exactly! We're both busy.

275
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:35,520
We hardly have time together.

276
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:37,840
Even we meet in the hospital,

277
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,200
we must pretend we don't know each other.

278
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:44,120
Come on...we knew this would happen, right?

279
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:51,880
It's getting dark. I think it will rain.

280
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:55,240
It's OK. We should still go.

281
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:56,480
Let's eat something good.

282
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,200
We can go anywhere.

283
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:01,400
But I asked a volunteer worker

284
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,680
to take Mary out in the sun.

285
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:05,720
I guess it won't happen now.

286
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:10,440
Mary told me you took good care of her.

287
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:11,880
She wanted me to thank you.

288
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:17,280
Cathy, how can I thank you?

289
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:21,680
I'm a nurse. It's my job to look
after my patients.

290
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:22,720
I'm not doing this for you.

291
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:29,600
I'm just worried Mary would
eventually find out about us.

292
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:30,960
She must be angry and heartbroken.

293
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:34,000
I'm afraid she won't let me
look after her again.

294
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:37,120
The things I said to encourage her
would go to waste.

295
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:41,360
You always think of others before yourself.

296
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:44,160
I should be the one to feel guilty.

297
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:48,160
Anway, today belongs to us.

298
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:49,600
Think of nothing else today.

299
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:52,360
Let's enjoy ourselves for the day, OK?

300
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,680
Shek? Why are you calling me?

301
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,640
Just tell your Boss to contact me.

302
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,160
No more games.

303
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,720
Ben? Who was it?

304
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,480
Nobody. Another phishing call.

305
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,080
Don't lie to me.

306
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:15,640
You're holding out on me.

307
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:18,920
You've been very secretive lately.

308
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,400
I can seldom get ahold of you

309
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,320
and you hardly visit Mary at the hospital.

310
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:26,000
I told you I'm busy at the bank.

311
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,400
What about the money in your account?

312
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:30,200
Sorry, I didn't mean to check on you.

313
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:30,760
But...

314
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:32,000
You're holding out on me too.

315
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,000
You hid the obstetrics check-up
report from me.

316
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:37,760
Are you pregnant?

317
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:40,880
I didn't mean to hide it from you...

318
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:43,080
I'll be a father...

319
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,440
No!

320
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,960
We agreed we won't have a baby.

321
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,760
I don't want to come between
you and Mary.

322
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,760
It's not your fault.

323
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:56,560
Even if it was an accident,

324
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,880
you can't possibly have an abortion.

325
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:01,800
At least that's my responsibility.

326
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,640
I don't want to add on to our burden.

327
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:09,720
You're already in debt because
of Mary's medical expenses.

328
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:13,640
That's why I need to make
a lot of money ASAP.

329
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:19,160
I want us to have a proper family.

330
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,960
Let's think this through carefully.

331
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:26,600
It's not just between us.

332
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:28,080
She's bound to find out.

333
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:31,800
It would be devastating to her.

334
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,680
Anyway, we must find a way to
continue to look after her

335
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:38,080
and give her enough money.

336
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,400
Keep her well-protected

337
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:41,800
so she won't worry about money again.

338
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:45,520
You talk about making a lot of money. How?

339
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:47,680
Are you doing something illegal?

340
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:51,240
No. Don't worry, I won't be reckless.

341
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:52,160
Nothing must happen to you...

342
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,640
It'll be OK.

343
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:56,320
I'm just exploiting loopholes in the law.

344
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,440
Trust me, I know what I'm doing.

345
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:02,280
This is a big deal.

346
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:03,880
Brother Kin, I want to know

347
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:06,240
this banker guy is always here.

348
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,720
What does he want?

349
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,560
He's always complaining.

350
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:11,080
Sounds like he's not happy with the cut.

351
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:13,080
Would he screw us up?

352
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,480
Rats!

353
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:17,040
Let's see who'd dare to piss off
Brother Kin.

354
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,400
We'd get even with him.

355
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,800
Yes, we have money now.

356
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:22,640
We'll go get grasshoppers

357
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,120
and cover his head with them.

358
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,800
You should hold him down

359
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,880
and cut open the top of his skull,

360
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,680
pour in mercury and then grasshoppers...

361
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:30,760
That sounds familiar...
It's itchy, right?

362
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:33,480
That sounds like fun.
Anything else more brutal?

363
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:34,160
More brutal?

364
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:36,000
Tie him up and leave him in the boonies

365
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:39,520
where there are loads of ants, insects,
snakes, wild boars...

366
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,800
plaster honey all over him

367
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:42,240
and let the insects feed on him.

368
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,720
When wild boars spot him...

369
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:48,440
Shut up! Enough of your nonsense.

370
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:53,560
He's a good citizen, unlike you two losers.

371
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,320
We're just kidding.

372
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:56,760
We're shooting the breeze.

373
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:59,320
People like him are easy to manage.

374
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,440
You can bluff him.

375
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:04,680
He's begging me to help him make some money.

376
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,040
He wouldn't dare play games.

377
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:08,360
Exactly! Don't worry about him.

378
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:09,840
Brother Kin is the boss.

379
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:13,040
We'll keep him on a leash and
the money will roll in.

380
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:16,120
You don't know anything.

381
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:18,200
Don't shoot off your mouth like those two.

382
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:20,960
I'm sorry.

383
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:25,000
I intend to treat you to a trip.

384
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:28,720
Really? I've never been on a plane before!

385
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:29,920
Me too.

386
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,280
You're in charge of planning this trip.

387
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,840
She'll decide what to do.

388
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:36,040
I'll check the flights right now.

389
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,600
Bravo, Boss...
Bravo, Brother Kin...

390
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:38,360
Bravo, Boss!

391
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:39,280
Bravo, Boss!

392
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:40,080
Bravo, Boss!

393
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:43,840
(A few days later)

394
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,360
It's been a week.

395
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,640
Ben hasn't been here for a week.

396
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,600
Maybe he'll come today.

397
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:54,920
It doesn't really matter.

398
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:57,000
I sent him a lot of messages,

399
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,600
but he didn't even read them.

400
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:03,320
Hello, we're with the CCB,
Commercial Crime Bureau.

401
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,480
Are you Mrs. Lau?

402
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:06,840
Yes, I am.

403
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,040
Your husband Lau Yue-bun,

404
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:11,280
is suspected of laundering money
for an underground casino.

405
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,920
We need you to facilitate our investigation.

406
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:15,760
Because of privacy reason,

407
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:18,440
we'd like you to step out for a minute.

408
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:21,000
Wait!

409
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:23,120
Nurse Tse is a good friend of mine.

410
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:26,080
I'd like her to stay. Is that OK?

411
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:30,280
When was the last time you saw your husband?

412
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:33,760
A week ago. Where is he now?

413
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,360
We have been trying to contact him

414
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:36,800
but to no avail so far.

415
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:39,280
You mean he's missing?

416
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:41,000
He didn't go to work?

417
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:44,120
That's not possible.

418
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:47,120
Mary, calm down. Take a deep breath.

419
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:49,040
Mrs. Lau, are you OK?

420
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:50,560
Can you continue?

421
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:54,360
Mrs. Lau, can you tell us

422
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:57,920
who has been in contact with
your husband lately?

423
00:20:58,280 --> 00:20:59,320
I have been hospitalized for a long time.

424
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:02,920
We have not been living the life
of an ordinary married couple.

425
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:06,040
He wouldn't tell me his problems.

426
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:08,040
I don't know what happened to him.

427
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,680
I really don't know.

428
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:13,120
But I believe Mr. Lau is a good man.

429
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,360
He would not do anything illegal.

430
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:18,280
We have reasons to believe
your husband has absconded.

431
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:19,880
If you hear from him,

432
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,080
please contact us right away.

433
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:23,560
If you find him...

434
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,880
Of course. We will let you know.

435
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,680
But you're in a hospital,

436
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:30,880
is it OK for you to take a call?

437
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:33,560
Or you can contact me.

438
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:37,720
You want the nurse to be your
emergency contact?

439
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:40,000
Ben and I have no family in Hong Kong.

440
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:42,440
Nurse Tse is a trusted friend.

441
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:00,000
Suet, why did you bring so much stuff?

442
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:01,880
I don't know how long we'll be gone.

443
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,200
Or where I can buy my things.

444
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:05,840
Hurry up! There's heavy traffic
going to the airport.

445
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:06,840
Sorry, Brother Kin.

446
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:08,920
Suet, carry your own suitcase.

447
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:11,640
Would Ben be here?

448
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,040
Nurse Tse?!

449
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:23,840
You're the girl from last time.

450
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:26,240
Yes, I borrowed $50 from you.

451
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:27,560
Let me pay you back.

452
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:30,400
That's OK.

453
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:32,880
Suet, it's time.

454
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:34,680
Go on ahead. I'll catch up.

455
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,360
No, come on.

456
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:36,120
Just go ahead.

457
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,680
Don't worry about the money.

458
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:39,640
You can pay me later.

459
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:40,920
Can you...

460
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:41,880
Suet, what's holding you up?

461
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:45,080
We have a plane to catch! Bye!

462
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:47,480
Hurry...

463
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:01,360
It's been a week. Where are you?

464
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,640
The Police came to see Mary.

465
00:23:03,960 --> 00:23:06,240
Is it about what you told me before?

466
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:09,680
I looked for you but couldn't find you.

467
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:12,280
Don't worry. I didn't say anything.

468
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:18,640
Text me, OK? I'm so worried about you.

469
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,480
I love you.

470
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:34,560
(Two weeks later)

471
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,320
If you wanted that suitcase,

472
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:36,960
you should have told me.

473
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:37,840
I'll buy it for you.

474
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:39,240
Don't fall for bargains.

475
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:41,040
Good thing you didn't apply for it.

476
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:43,680
OK, I'll tell you next time.

477
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:45,920
But those two have gone too far.

478
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:48,200
When I saw online the victims of the scam

479
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:49,760
mentioned applying for a virtual credit card

480
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:50,960
I knew those two were involved.

481
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:54,800
Let's go expose them now.

482
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,200
Which one?

483
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:04,040
I saw them moving something right here.

484
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:06,440
But I wasn't sure which unit they came from.

485
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:10,200
What's that stench?

486
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:15,440
Smells like rotten meat.

487
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:17,840
Hello?

488
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:20,240
Hello?

489
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:33,800
Hello?

490
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,400
Is this Miss Tse Chi-kwan?

491
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:36,600
Speaking.

492
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:38,720
This is the New Territories East
Crime Unit.

493
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,040
You have news about Ben?

494
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:42,560
Yes, we found Mr. Lau Yue-bun.

495
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:45,360
Unfortunately, he is dead.

496
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:45,800
What?

497
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:50,160
A few days ago, a couple went to
the 9/F of Po Fat Industrial Building.

498
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:52,320
The guy is a reporter.

499
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:55,360
He was looking into a scam that involved
promoting a fake credit card.

500
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:58,840
They smelled a stench when they
walked past one of the units.

501
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:01,600
They knocked on the door but
no one answered.

502
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,600
The Police arrived at the scene

503
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:04,640
and broke the door down

504
00:25:04,840 --> 00:25:06,920
to discover the air con was
turned on full blast,

505
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:09,520
the air was filled with the smell of

506
00:25:09,560 --> 00:25:12,880
mothballs, air freshener and Chinese herbs.

507
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,520
In the middle of the unit,

508
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:16,840
we found a wooden crate about
half a person's height.

509
00:25:17,360 --> 00:25:18,600
We pried the crate open

510
00:25:18,840 --> 00:25:20,680
and found a stone coffin inside.

511
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:24,080
The Fire Services tried to open it

512
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:25,680
but the cement was too hard.

513
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:28,320
It took them a long time to open it

514
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:31,400
and we found the body of a man inside.

515
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:35,200
The body has decomposed.

516
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:37,000
We checked the DNA

517
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:39,480
and confirmed it was Mr. Lau Yue-bun.

518
00:25:40,040 --> 00:25:41,560
The initial autopsy report indicated

519
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:44,680
the estimated time of death
was two to three weeks ago.

520
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:47,200
We found multiple injuries on the body
from a fight.

521
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:51,120
The cause of death was a fatal blow
to the hindbrain by a nail.

522
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:59,520
Ben...how is this possible? Ben...

523
00:25:59,560 --> 00:26:00,200
Mary...

524
00:26:00,960 --> 00:26:02,000
Ben...

525
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:05,760
You can identify the body through
the screen behind you.

526
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:08,040
I must warn you, be prepared...

527
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:09,760
the decomposition of the body

528
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,120
made him beyond recognition.

529
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:16,880
Mrs. Lau, do these belong to your husband?

530
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:27,760
Ben...how could you leave me?

531
00:26:29,840 --> 00:26:32,040
How could you leave me like this?

532
00:26:33,320 --> 00:26:36,560
Mary, I know you're heartbroken,

533
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:38,440
but you must mind your health.

534
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:43,720
Ben is gone, I don't want to be alone here.

535
00:26:44,200 --> 00:26:46,160
I don't want to be alone here.

536
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:49,400
No, you're not alone.

537
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:50,960
You still have me.

538
00:26:52,280 --> 00:26:56,480
Don't worry, I'll take care of you for Ben.

539
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:05,680
Miss Tse, when was the last time
you saw Mr. Lau Yue-bun?

540
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:09,000
About three weeks ago

541
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:11,920
when Mr. Lau visited his wife.

542
00:27:12,400 --> 00:27:15,360
We chatted about Mary's condition.

543
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:19,240
You seem quite close to them.

544
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:21,960
Mary has been staying at Ming Sum Hospital
for three years.

545
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:23,920
Mr. Lau visited her often.

546
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:26,240
Naturally, we got acquainted.

547
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:28,880
The last Tuesday of last month at 3:30pm

548
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:29,720
what were you doing?

549
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:31,800
I don't remember.

550
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:33,080
I need to check my schedule.

551
00:27:33,400 --> 00:27:34,400
I might be at work.

552
00:27:34,480 --> 00:27:37,880
No need. The CCTV nearby

553
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:40,400
saw you near Po Fat Industrial Building.

554
00:27:40,720 --> 00:27:42,600
What were you doing there?

555
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:47,200
I went looking for Mr. Lau.

556
00:27:47,760 --> 00:27:51,400
After officers from the CCB
dropped by earlier,

557
00:27:51,720 --> 00:27:53,720
I remembered for some time,

558
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:57,920
Mr. Lau always bought dessert
for Mary from Sweetness.

559
00:27:58,200 --> 00:28:00,160
Sweetness has no other branches.

560
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:02,200
The only shop is near
Po Fat Industrial Building.

561
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:06,960
That place is not near where
Mr. Lau worked or lived.

562
00:28:07,640 --> 00:28:09,680
He must have a reason for going there.

563
00:28:10,120 --> 00:28:11,760
I decided to try my luck

564
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:12,880
and see if I would run into him.

565
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:16,080
You seem know Mr. Lau very well

566
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:17,280
and are aware of his whereabouts.

567
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:20,400
You claim to be friends with Mrs. Lau.

568
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:22,560
Are you so close you'd help her
look for her husband?

569
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:25,560
When you identified the body,

570
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:27,080
I heard you tell Mrs. Lau,

571
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:29,000
you'd take care of her for Ben.

572
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:33,640
What makes you feel you have
such an obligation?

573
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,480
For Ben or for Mary?

574
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:38,040
They're the same to me.

575
00:28:39,080 --> 00:28:39,880
They are equally close?

576
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:42,400
Let me ask you this...

577
00:28:42,840 --> 00:28:47,760
Do you know why Mr. Lau is suddenly
involved in the underground casino

578
00:28:47,880 --> 00:28:49,280
and might be helping someone launder money?

579
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:52,040
I only know Ben is not a greedy man.

580
00:28:52,360 --> 00:28:55,200
Mary's illness has been a heavy
financial burden for him.

581
00:28:55,720 --> 00:28:56,320
Besides...

582
00:28:57,560 --> 00:28:59,280
Miss Tse, level with us.

583
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:01,880
What's your relationship with Lau Yue-bun?

584
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:06,680
Ben and I have been together for two years.

585
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:10,280
We started a year after
Mary was hospitalized.

586
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:44,560
Come on, 1...2...3...

587
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:48,600
Careful!

588
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:13,640
I'm so useless...
Don't say that...

589
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:20,320
Sir, are you OK?

590
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:22,920
I can't take this anymore.

591
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:33,240
I know. Many patients with
rare diseases are like that.

592
00:30:33,760 --> 00:30:34,960
Just follow the doctor's orders.

593
00:30:35,440 --> 00:30:36,360
There's a way.

594
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:14,600
Cathy!

595
00:31:18,920 --> 00:31:23,240
I've been thinking, let's just break up.

596
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:27,440
Mary is so nice I don't want to hurt her.

597
00:31:30,120 --> 00:31:31,600
But I don't want to lose you.

598
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:42,600
During the two years you were together,

599
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:44,400
you've been taking care of Mrs. Lau.

600
00:31:46,880 --> 00:31:48,080
You really don't mind?

601
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:51,600
You never asked Mr. Lau to divorce his wife?

602
00:31:52,120 --> 00:31:54,840
No. Ben never wanted to.

603
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:57,440
They have a good relationship.

604
00:31:58,160 --> 00:32:01,080
Mrs. Lau never knew about your affair?

605
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:03,200
We didn't want to hurt her

606
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:05,040
or let this affect her health.

607
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:08,000
We kept it from her. She didn't know.

608
00:32:09,760 --> 00:32:11,640
When Ben said he was exploiting
loopholes in the law,

609
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:13,160
I believed him.

610
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:14,800
Only after he disappeared,

611
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:16,040
I realized there was more to it.

612
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:18,720
I wanna know...

613
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:21,760
If I told you sooner, would he have died?

614
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:25,200
At least we'll try hard to catch the killer.

615
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:28,320
That's all I know.

616
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:30,720
If I think of anything else,

617
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:32,480
I'll be in touch.

618
00:32:33,080 --> 00:32:35,240
The CCB busted the underground casino

619
00:32:35,360 --> 00:32:36,960
and confiscated the dirty money.

620
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:41,400
But we're still tracking down the $1.8M

621
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:43,240
Lau Yue-bun received for money laundering.

622
00:32:43,600 --> 00:32:46,480
You talk about making a lot of money. How?

623
00:32:46,760 --> 00:32:47,760
Are you doing something illegal?

624
00:32:48,360 --> 00:32:50,200
We didn't find his phone at the scene.

625
00:32:50,720 --> 00:32:54,040
We checked with the telecom company

626
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:54,920
but found nothing from his phone log.

627
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:57,720
Do you know what happened to the money?

628
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:00,640
No. I have no idea.

629
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:07,840
Miss Tse, what you told us just now,

630
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:08,880
we'll keep it confidential

631
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:10,200
and won't tell Mrs. Lau.

632
00:33:12,120 --> 00:33:13,400
Thank you, Gogo Sir.

633
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:31,240
According to the CCB,

634
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:33,640
a gang of criminals lead by Tai Yat-kin

635
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:37,240
was helping a local illegal gambling
syndicate with money laundering.

636
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:40,480
Lau Yue-bun used his authority in the bank

637
00:33:40,680 --> 00:33:44,080
falsified records and opened
a dozen fake accounts

638
00:33:44,400 --> 00:33:47,160
and helped them launder money.

639
00:33:47,480 --> 00:33:48,200
What about these four?

640
00:33:48,520 --> 00:33:51,560
Tai Yat-kin, Cheung Sai-chor,
Hung Wai-shek and Ho Pui-suet?

641
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:52,960
Any sign of them?

642
00:33:53,320 --> 00:33:55,960
We checked the CCTV at Po Fat
Industrial Building.

643
00:33:56,120 --> 00:33:56,800
Before and after the incident,

644
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:58,680
they have all been coming in and out
of the building,

645
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:03,120
with Cheung Sai-chor and Hung Wai-shek
made the most trips.

646
00:34:03,560 --> 00:34:06,520
We also found out they bought
plane tickets in advance.

647
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:07,680
They must be on the run.

648
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:09,960
I'm 80% sure they did it.

649
00:34:10,280 --> 00:34:12,240
They bought plane tickets in advance,

650
00:34:12,440 --> 00:34:14,280
that means it was premeditated.

651
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:17,320
I bet they argued over divvying up the loot

652
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:18,720
and they killed him on the spot.

653
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:21,480
They're vicious, but stupid.

654
00:34:21,880 --> 00:34:24,920
The stone coffin is too heavy to move.

655
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:26,960
It'll be discovered eventually.

656
00:34:27,320 --> 00:34:29,000
What a shame they got away.

657
00:34:29,240 --> 00:34:30,720
What about the wife and the lover?

658
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:31,800
Anything from them?

659
00:34:32,240 --> 00:34:33,880
The wife looks clean.

660
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:35,520
But the mistress is a bit fishy.

661
00:34:37,160 --> 00:34:38,520
In what way?

662
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:42,640
Just think, a decent girl willingly
became the mistress

663
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:44,160
and took such good care of the wife.

664
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:45,200
How is that possible?

665
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:46,600
What do you suspect?

666
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:50,720
The guy used the mistress to
look after the wife,

667
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:53,040
or the mistress used the wife
to keep the guy,

668
00:34:53,160 --> 00:34:54,560
or the wife is...

669
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:56,160
Hey...you're overthinking.

670
00:34:56,520 --> 00:34:58,440
Any kinky relationship is possible
in this world.

671
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:00,160
A love triangle is relatively
simple already.

672
00:35:00,200 --> 00:35:01,960
The guy needs consolation,

673
00:35:02,160 --> 00:35:04,240
the wife needs care

674
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:06,160
and the mistress needs love.

675
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:10,480
To each his own.

676
00:35:10,720 --> 00:35:14,360
If there's mutual consent,
even a love octagon is OK, right?

677
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:18,240
Oh, samosa!

678
00:35:18,560 --> 00:35:20,120
What kind of relationship is that?

679
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:22,120
They have samosa for afternoon tea today.

680
00:35:22,160 --> 00:35:23,440
You can still get it if you go down now.

681
00:35:23,600 --> 00:35:25,960
What do you want? Text me.

682
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:27,720
Thanks, Brother Bo...

683
00:35:29,520 --> 00:35:32,360
Get some rest. I'll fetch your meds.

684
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:38,960
How do you want Ben's funeral?

685
00:35:39,240 --> 00:35:40,280
I'll do it the way you want.

686
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:48,080
What flowers should we use
in the mourning hall?

687
00:35:53,120 --> 00:35:55,000
I'll let you decide.

688
00:35:57,840 --> 00:36:00,880
I think you'll pick jasmine.

689
00:36:02,720 --> 00:36:03,480
Why?

690
00:36:06,080 --> 00:36:09,880
Actually, I knew about you and Ben.

691
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:19,080
Honey, this is for you.

692
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:21,400
Why jasmine?

693
00:36:21,760 --> 00:36:24,080
I don't know. I like the smell lately.

694
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:33,200
It smells good. What is it?

695
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:35,400
You can smell it? It's jasmine.

696
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:36,600
I'm into jasmine lately.

697
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,160
Last night, I saw a movie called

698
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:43,360
Next Decision to Leave. It's quite good.

699
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:46,520
What did you do yesterday on your day off?

700
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:49,800
Me? I saw a movie,

701
00:36:49,960 --> 00:36:52,640
called Next Decision to Leave. It's good.

702
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,800
Maybe I was too sensitive.

703
00:36:55,280 --> 00:36:57,920
But I'm not surprised at all.

704
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:02,440
I'm sorry, Mary! I'm so sorry...

705
00:37:02,640 --> 00:37:04,320
I'm telling you not because I blame you.

706
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:06,520
Now that Ben is gone,

707
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:08,480
there's no need to hide it.

708
00:37:09,040 --> 00:37:11,120
You must hate me, right?

709
00:37:12,400 --> 00:37:16,480
No woman would want her husband
to be with another woman.

710
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,560
I was heartbroken.

711
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:22,400
But I'm not angry with you two.

712
00:37:23,080 --> 00:37:25,200
For two years, I saw how Ben changed

713
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:27,800
from a living corpse to someone
who can smile again.

714
00:37:28,200 --> 00:37:29,720
If you weren't there for him,

715
00:37:29,960 --> 00:37:31,320
I'm sure he couldn't take it anymore.

716
00:37:32,640 --> 00:37:36,040
Ben was a good man and deserved to be happy.

717
00:37:36,480 --> 00:37:38,120
If he was alive,

718
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:41,840
you two could have been very happy.

719
00:37:42,280 --> 00:37:45,560
No, we want what's best for you.

720
00:37:45,600 --> 00:37:48,320
I'm so sorry. It was my fault.

721
00:37:48,480 --> 00:37:49,880
I failed to control my feelings.

722
00:37:50,040 --> 00:37:52,040
Luckily you failed.

723
00:37:52,520 --> 00:37:56,800
Ben was at least happy towards
the end of his life.

724
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:59,920
Look at me...there was nothing I could do.

725
00:38:00,400 --> 00:38:03,840
I couldn't take care of him
or make him happy.

726
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:06,760
I thought about killing myself.

727
00:38:07,120 --> 00:38:11,480
Because I saw how happy Ben was
thanks to you

728
00:38:11,840 --> 00:38:13,240
I didn't feel so hopeless.

729
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:18,520
You saved him and you saved me too.

730
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:23,320
No, we only want you to be happy.

731
00:38:23,800 --> 00:38:25,920
I'm so sorry...

732
00:38:26,160 --> 00:38:27,760
Please let me look after you.

733
00:38:28,680 --> 00:38:30,000
Don't try to console me.

734
00:38:32,080 --> 00:38:34,800
You must feel awful over Ben's death.

735
00:38:36,880 --> 00:38:39,840
You must be tired from hiding the truth.

736
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:41,520
It must have been tough, right?

737
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:46,360
You can let it out now. Go ahead and cry.

738
00:38:51,520 --> 00:38:52,920
I'm so sorry...

739
00:39:19,600 --> 00:39:22,520
Cathy, your shift ended. You're still here?

740
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:25,720
I'm filling in for Linda.

741
00:39:26,040 --> 00:39:27,920
But you just came off the graveyard shift.

742
00:39:28,120 --> 00:39:28,720
Can you manage?

743
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:30,320
I'm OK.

744
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:32,280
OK, I'm leaving.

745
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:33,200
Bye!

746
00:39:33,600 --> 00:39:35,160
Almost forgot my phone. Bye!

747
00:39:52,520 --> 00:39:55,040
For two years, I saw how Ben changed

748
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:57,480
from a living corpse to someone
who can smile again.

749
00:39:58,000 --> 00:39:59,360
If you weren't there for him,

750
00:39:59,400 --> 00:40:01,000
I'm sure he couldn't take it anymore.

751
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:05,920
Ben was a good man and deserved to be happy.

752
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:07,800
If he was alive,

753
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:11,560
you two could have been very happy.

754
00:40:38,120 --> 00:40:40,320
Suet, can you stop pushing the button?

755
00:40:40,520 --> 00:40:42,800
Don't stand over there.

756
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:43,600
Push where?

757
00:40:43,640 --> 00:40:47,000
It's infra-red, genius! Move!

758
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:48,920
Quiet! You're getting on my nerves.

759
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:51,560
God knows how long we're stuck here.

760
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:54,960
I'm going crazy! Out of my way!

761
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:16,040
Suet, where are you going?

762
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:18,640
Where are you off to at this hour?

763
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:19,560
Brother Kin...

764
00:41:19,800 --> 00:41:22,640
Don't call him. I'm very hungry.

765
00:41:25,040 --> 00:41:27,480
Hungry? You just finished eating.

766
00:41:27,760 --> 00:41:29,160
Cup noodles can't fill me up.

767
00:41:29,200 --> 00:41:31,600
I'm sick of cup noodles for every meal.

768
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:33,600
We spent all our money.

769
00:41:33,640 --> 00:41:36,600
What else can we eat?

770
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:38,240
Who knew we'd be stuck in here for so long?

771
00:41:38,560 --> 00:41:40,360
I'm going to run out for a minute.

772
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:48,760
Come on, I'll get you something, OK?

773
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,160
I don't know...what do you think?

774
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:54,000
OK...but don't spend all your money.

775
00:41:54,040 --> 00:41:54,840
We don't have much left.

776
00:41:55,040 --> 00:41:56,120
OK, I know.

777
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:11,520
Come in!

778
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:13,160
Ching Sir, we got something.

779
00:42:13,560 --> 00:42:14,000
What?

780
00:42:14,280 --> 00:42:17,200
Just got word, a Hong Kong girl in her 20s

781
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:18,440
showed up at the Wanchai precinct

782
00:42:18,600 --> 00:42:20,280
and claimed she was Suet from
the stone coffin case.

783
00:42:20,320 --> 00:42:21,680
Of her own free will?

784
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:23,240
Yes. She came to turn herself in.
